; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
;
; CAN RX edge-pair capture.
;
; X free-runs downward, one decrement every two cycles.  Every edge samples
; the low 16 bits of X into the ISR; autopush at 32 bits therefore emits one
; word per pair of edges:
;
;   word[31:16] = X[15:0] at the 1->0 edge
;   word[15:0]  = X[15:0] at the following 0->1 edge
;
; The host turns consecutive 16-bit timestamps into deltas (mod 2^16) and
; carries them on a 31-bit virtual down-counter for can_edge_sm.  Any gap
; inside a frame is at most a few bit times, so the 16-bit counter cannot
; wrap there.  The idle gap before SOF may wrap, which is harmless: only the
; SOF start uses it, and can_edge_sm rebases there.
;
; The edge path is two cycles with no `jmp x--`, while the steady loop
; decrements once per two cycles.  Every captured edge therefore leaves X one
; count high relative to a free-running clock, so every gap measures one tick
; short.  Both directions are symmetric, so can_edge_pair adds back a single
; constant (+1 tick per edge) instead of the old program's four-cycle path,
; which lost two.  Without that bias the bit clock drifts about one tick per
; edge and a frame eventually drops a bit.
;
; The SM is armed while the bus is recessive and starts at `high_cnt`, so the
; first captured 1->0 is SOF.  If the bus is already dominant when the SM is
; enabled (an edge slipped in during the arming sequence), that first capture
; uses the enable-time counter value instead of the true edge.  That frame is
; lost to CRC, but the parser resets at the next SOF and later frames are
; unaffected.  The first field is a 1->0 either way, so pairs stay aligned.
;
; Both steady loops are two instructions, so the tick is two cycles.  `jmp
; x--` with X == 0 is not taken and writes 0xFFFFFFFF; the instruction after
; each count loop is that loop's head, so the 32-bit underflow re-enters with
; no extra instruction.  The one exception is `low_cnt`, whose head is before
; it, so its underflow falls through a `jmp low`.  That jump runs once per
; 2^32 ticks (~68 s), never in a normal bit, and inverting the low test is not
; possible: PIO JMP has no `!pin` condition.  Using the wrap for `low_cnt`
; instead saves that word but makes the low capture skip a different number
; of decrements than the high capture, which breaks the single-bias model.
;
; X needs no initialisation: an edge reached before the first decrement just
; samples the existing value.

.program can_rx_pair
high_cnt:
    jmp x--, high        ; X was 0: X=0xFFFFFFFF, fall through into high
.wrap_target
high:
    jmp pin, high_cnt    ; still recessive: count
    in x, 16             ; 1->0, upper half; falls into low
low:
    jmp pin, low_cap     ; 0->1
low_cnt:
    jmp x--, low         ; X was 0: fall through
    jmp low
low_cap:
    in x, 16             ; 0->1, lower half -> autopush
.wrap                    ; back to high
